{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"obeliskoid-indigoid-egg","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observed (2026-10-27 ~21:50–22:05 PDT, while implementing story `6b66-9378-ebb1-446c`)\n\nCarried forward from `dc9b-e792-bad3-4578` (refreshing-cosmic-jaeger), which is closing because its confirmed defect (completion dedup key without material) was already fixed on main by `f147e08242f`. This symptom was NOT explained there and is not a de-dup failure.\n\n- `set_file_impact` 13 → 14 paths, then a non-forced `review_plan_start` returned a BLOCK whose `durable.verdict` was `stale-material` and whose `signed_at` was the *previous* run's.\n- `show_ticket` reported `plan_reviews: 0` — no findings were produced, so no fresh review ran.\n- `review_plan_start(force=True)` on the identical tree and SHA (`ee5253abfd4`) returned a certified PASS.\n- `gate_status` simultaneously reported `status: \"passed\"` and `findings.readable: true` for the BLOCK job, so the two surfaces an agent uses to sanity-check disagreed.\n\n## Ruled out\n\n- **De-dup.** The two starts returned different job ids (`…dbe7ada2`, `…41c67599`); a de-duplicated start returns the existing job's id. The plan-review dedup variant has carried the material fingerprint since `864b6f56c91`.\n- `stale-material` is produced only inside attestation *validation* (`llm/plan_review/attest.py`), comparing the recorded attestation against current material — so the returned `signed_at` is the step-2 attestation being reported stale, not a replayed run.\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven)\n\n1. **A reuse short-circuit fired.** `llm/plan_review/__init__.py` calls `reuse.idempotent_reuse` then `reuse.verdict_reuse`; both are bypassed by `force`, matching the force/no-force asymmetry. On reading, neither should fire (`idempotent_reuse` returns `None` when `claim_gate_check` is not ok; `verdict_reuse` requires the stored sidecar's `material_fingerprint` to match). If one fired, the bug is in its guard.\n2. **A precheck ahead of the LLM** returned the validation result directly, which explains the empty findings and the replayed `signed_at` without any reuse path firing.\n\n## Experiment\n\nBoth produce the same observable payload, so static reading cannot separate them. Reproduce with the existing test seams (a fake `rebar.llm.review_plan` and a real temp store): sign a plan-review attestation, change `file_impact`, call `review_plan_start` without force, and record which of `idempotent_reuse`, `verdict_reuse`, or a pre-LLM precheck returned the result. Only if the seams cannot reach the path, spend one instrumented real run.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The mechanism that returned the stale-material BLOCK without findings is identified with a reproducing test.\n- [ ] A non-forced re-review after a material edit produces its own findings (or a clearly labelled stale-attestation result that `gate_status` does not report as a passed run with readable findings).\n- [ ] Regression test pins that behaviour.","id":"c3c0-0b27-a2eb-4084","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["mcp","plan-review-gate","correctness"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Non-forced review_plan_start after a material edit returns the prior stale-material BLOCK with no findings"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793494036718068001,"uuid":"c41fefee-cf02-4f1c-846b-cd2bccce3f62"}